# deploy/Caddyfile — BASE (global options only) for the 165.99.219.35 box.
#
# The live Caddyfile on the server is assembled by deploy/scripts/remote-proxy.sh:
#
#     this file (global options)
#   + every "# >>> <site> >>> … # <<< <site> <<<" block already on the server
#     that belongs to ANOTHER site (e.g. debtbooktracker.com)
#   + deploy/caddy-site.snippet   (this site's block, __DOMAIN__ substituted)
#
# That is why the taxhelperbd.com block no longer lives here — it moved to
# deploy/caddy-site.snippet. One Caddy container fronts several sites, and each
# repo must be able to update its own block without deleting anyone else's.
# Editing this file changes global options only.
#
# Caddy fetches + auto-renews a free Let's Encrypt cert per site (DNS for each
# host must already point at this server; ports 80 + 443 open).
#
# The container is started by remote-proxy.sh only when none is running:
#   docker run -d --name bd-tax-caddy --restart unless-stopped \
#     --network bd-tax-network -p 80:80 -p 443:443 \
#     -e DEPLOY_DOMAIN=taxhelperbd.com \
#     -v caddy_data:/data -v caddy_config:/config \
#     -v /home/deploy/bd-tax-caddy/Caddyfile:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile:ro \
#     caddy:2 caddy run --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
{
	# Let's Encrypt expiry notices. Override with DEPLOY_ACME_EMAIL in deploy/.env.
	email {$DEPLOY_ACME_EMAIL:contact.marufalam@gmail.com}
}
